-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by Jon Attree in JNext through the real loader,
              2026-11-04

  Replay      52 normalized-time lockstep runs, 141000 frames: 18 default-
              colour (48000), 16 scenery-only (45000), 18 Smooth scrolling
              (48000); all game-state comparisons IDENTICAL. Smooth picture
              checks: 29550 interrupt frames, zero offset/tile/sprite/clip
              differences. Existing 12 negative cases detected; six new rules
              tested: sound-clock, speed-restore, missing-cap, early-sprite-
              commit, premature-pattern-upload and four-pixel catch-up jump;
              all controls detected. All 467 figure cases pass with smoothing
              off and on, including mirrored and multipart figures; eight
              existing figure-unit negatives also detected. Pure drawing
              wrappers preserve registers, memory and incoming CPU clock in 20
              cases at all four speeds. Replay normalizes hook time and skips
              only the isolated video-line wait; native JNext tests that wait
              independently.

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless. Pace target SLOWDOWN REMOVED: drawing at
              28 MHz, game logic and sound at 3.5 MHz; cap of 1244 video lines
              before the player update. Ten trials per quiet/busy scene.
              Original 12.37/11.19 updates/s; prior colour 12.01/10.52; new
              default 12.34/12.33. Native sound and restored-clock checks
              pass; AY sequence and tempo match after start-phase alignment.
              Smooth commits tilemap, pattern uploads and sprite attributes
              together. Native tilemap/sprite alignment 1125/1125 video
              frames; early-commit negative fails 66. The generic ULA flicker
              checker has one warning on the opaque-tilemap build; its frame
              was inspected and the actual tilemap agrees. Host reconstruction
              is byte-exact for both targets with both toggle choices. Menu
              startup preserves all 40 banks, registers (except R), MMU and
              stack in four toggle/IFF cases; both menu choices reach play in
              headless JNext. These checks are rerun after packaging and
              recorded beside this patch.

  Coverage    Worlds 1-5 and six boss-level start states, retaining the
              previous patch's short-play and unit-tested-boss limits. The
              stage-1 multiload payload, source targets and trainers are
              retained. No new complete-game playthrough is claimed. Real-time
              encounters can differ because the original IRQ mixes interrupted
              A into its RNG; no LD A,R instruction was found in the game
              banks.

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
